# ===========================================================================
# Robot Brawl API — build context exclusions.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS NOT A SPEED OPTIMISATION. Without it the image build is likely to
# FAIL, and the reason is not obvious from the Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile restores inside the container first (for layer caching), then
# does `COPY RobotBrawl.Api/ RobotBrawl.Api/`. With no exclusions that COPY
# drags the HOST's obj/ over the container's freshly restored one — and the
# host's obj/project.assets.json is full of absolute macOS paths:
#
#     /Users/leondu/.nuget/packages/
#     /Users/leondu/Setup Guide In-Editor Tutorial/server/RobotBrawl.Api/...
#
# Six of them. Inside a Linux container none of those exist, so the publish
# that follows either fails outright or builds against stale host artifacts.
# Copying host bin/ over the container's output has the same shape of problem.
#
# Found by inspection rather than by building, because no container runtime is
# installed on this machine — see docs. The image build itself remains
# UNPROVEN; this removes one known reason it would not work.
# ===========================================================================

# Build output — regenerated inside the container, never copied in.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Test artifacts and their build output. The API image has no use for the
# bench suite, and glicko_check is a second csproj that would confuse a
# directory-wide restore.
tests/
qa_*.txt
qa_*.log

# Local state that must never enter an image.
*.local
.env
